  "result": "Still checking the archive. I've found no past ticket for this exact problem, so I'm giving my conclusion now.\n\n{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no earlier ticket reporting this problem. The archive has no report of the Startup page's \\\"Launch at login\\\" setting being disabled by an OS setting without showing a reason. Older tickets about startup (#12564, #14820, #18455, #10699) cover other problems, such as the setting being ignored or not persisting. This looks like a new regression from the PR you mentioned (#20200). The localized reason text already exists, so the fix is to show it again when the setting is disabled. Please keep this ticket open as a new bug. In the meantime, you can check or change the startup state in Windows Settings > Apps > Startup.\"}",
